ion *plus* the data that describes it.** Two things can have the same resolution but completely different picture quality because the data describing the pixels is different. **In short: "1080p" is a measure of quantity, not quality.** You are right that the quantity is the same. But the quality of the data filling that quantity is what makes the difference in data usage and, if you look closely, the picture itself.
