ixels it receives from Stadia, even though both are labeled "1080p." The resolution is the same (same number of pixels), but the *data describing those pixels* is different. One is high-quality data, the other is lower-quality data. Your screen faithfully displays the difference. **In short: "1080p" tells you the *quantity* of pixels. It does not tell you the *quality* of the data describing those pixels.** That's why two 1080p streams can look different.
